Validation Metric: 0.8804

-------------------------------
Design: I propose to integrate sample weighting based on skin tone frequency into the LightGBM training to further reduce fairness gaps. During each CV fold and the final training, we compute per-sample weights using `compute_sample_weight('balanced', skin_tones)` so that underrepresented tones are upweighted. All other parts of the pipeline (efficientnet feature extraction, triple TTA, evaluation) remain unchanged. This should help balance performance across skin tones without sacrificing overall AUROC.
