Design: I propose to extend the TTA scheme by adding a deterministic 90° rotation alongside the existing horizontal and vertical flips, and to train the LightGBM classifier directly on the average of all four embeddings (orig, h-flip, v-flip, rot-90) rather than only the original features. This way the model learns on the richer, augmented feature space, which should boost robustness and AUROC. We will extract embeddings under the four transforms, average them, run 5-fold CV on these averaged features (printing overall AUROC and light/dark gap), retrain on the full averaged embeddings, and update the `predict()` function to include the rotation in its TTA.
